\newlabel{fig:greedyfail}{{7.8}{86}{Three plausible greedy rules and their counterexamples. Interval scheduling needs the earliest \emph {end}; coin change needs dynamic programming unless the coin system is special (such as $1, 2, 5, 10, \ldots $)}{figure.caption.119}{}}
